  "gold_standard_summary": "## Patient Summary — John Smith (DOB: 1990-03-15, Male)\n\n**Chief Concern / Visit Type:** Annual preventive physical examination.\n\n**Active Conditions:**\n- Essential hypertension (I10), diagnosed June 2022, currently well-controlled on Lisinopril.\n\n**Medications (2):**\n1. Lisinopril 10 mg daily (hypertension)\n2. Vitamin D 2,000 IU daily (supplementation)\n\n**Allergies:** No known allergies (NKA).\n\n**Recent Labs (2025-11-15):**\n- Total Cholesterol: 195 mg/dL (borderline; no statin indicated at this time)\n- LDL: 115 mg/dL\n- HbA1c: 5.4% (normal — no diabetes)\n- eGFR: 82 mL/min (normal kidney function)\n\n**Vitals (2025-11-15):** BP 128/82 mmHg (improved), BMI 24.5 (normal weight).\n\n**Immunizations:** Flu vaccine 2025-10-01 (current); COVID-19 booster 2024-09-15.\n\n**Clinical Impression:** Healthy 35-year-old male with controlled hypertension. No diabetic risk at this time. Cholesterol borderline — lifestyle counseling recommended. Continue Lisinopril and annual follow-up.\n\n---\n⚠️ DRAFT — AI-GENERATED — REQUIRES CLINICIAN REVIEW",
